Now, we will bootstrap the system by copying a base ArchLinux install to the
mounted partitions (or subvolumes to be more precise). Normally, this base
system consists of three packages: base, linux and linux-firmware.

However, we will extend the base install by a couple of packages that will be
useful later on. If you wish, you may switch out linux with a different kernel
package. You may also specify additional packages, you want to install on your
system.
